{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CggBfXjRB19H6gz3NqgEB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Result:** Dq ≈ 740 cm⁻¹, B ≈ 953 cm⁻¹, C ≈ 2190 cm⁻¹. B and C rest on two simplifications that I did not check against the full matrices. These are the trace rule for the ³T₁ pair and neglect of configuration mixing for ¹E.\n\nThe bands are the spin-allowed transitions from the ³A₂(F) ground state, plus the spin-forbidden ¹E band.\n\n1. **Dq.** The lowest band is the ³A₂ → ³T₂ transition, which is 10Dq. So 10Dq = 7400 cm⁻¹ and Dq = 740 cm⁻¹.\n\n2. **B.** The two ³T₁ states (F and P) mix through a 2×2 matrix. The sum of its two eigenvalues, measured from the ground state, equals the trace. This trace is 15B + 30Dq, which I took from the weak-field and strong-field limits rather than deriving the full matrix. It gives:\n   - ν₂ + ν₃ = 12 660 + 23 840 = 36 500 cm⁻¹\n   - 15B = 36 500 − 30(740) = 14 300 cm⁻¹\n   - B ≈ 953 cm⁻¹\n\n3. **C.** The ¹E state arises from the same t₂⁶e² configuration as the ground state. I took the ¹E − ³A₂ gap as 9B + 3C. This neglects mixing with other ¹E states.\n   - 15 150 = 9(953) + 3C = 8580 + 3C\n   - C ≈ 2190 cm⁻¹\n\nThe resulting C/B ≈ 2.3 is a reasonable value.\n\n{\"Dq\": 740, \"B\": 953, \"C\": 2190, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Dq from ν1/10; B from the ³T₁ trace rule (ν2+ν3 = 15B+30Dq); C from ¹E = 9B+3C, neglecting configuration mixing of ¹E.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1704,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1704,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3c1acd36-de11-4336-b4ae-c1715986fcae","uuid":"3ed1a13f-642a-4ba1-9